From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <bap@debian.org>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: confshared.h ppc64

Fix two 64-bit PowerPC problems in confshared.h

First: gcc defines __powerpc__ on both 32-bit and 64-bit PowerPC, so
on ppc64el both the __ppc__ and the __ppc64__ blocks were included, so
MACHINE_TYPE and CURRENT_FASL_ARCH were each defined twice. The
microcode is built with -Werror, so on ppc64el every file that
includes confshared.h failed:

  error: 'MACHINE_TYPE' redefined [-Werror]
  error: 'CURRENT_FASL_ARCH' redefined [-Werror]

Fix: guard the 32-bit definitions with !defined(__powerpc64__).

Second: confshared.h should define HEAP_IN_LOW_MEMORY on 64-bit
PowerPC, but the __ppc64__ block set only MACHINE_TYPE and
CURRENT_FASL_ARCH, while __x86_64__ and __aarch64__ also set
HEAP_IN_LOW_MEMORY. (That was masked because of issue above which
loaded the 32-bit PowerPC block which does define it.)

Fix: define HEAP_IN_LOW_MEMORY in the 64-bit PowePC block.
---
 src/microcode/confshared.h | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/microcode/confshared.h b/src/microcode/confshared.h
index 2aca540..c27f209 100644
--- a/src/microcode/confshared.h
+++ b/src/microcode/confshared.h
@@ -568,7 +568,10 @@ extern void win32_stack_reset (void);
 #define MAX_FLONUM_EXPONENT    1023
 #endif
 
-#ifdef __powerpc__
+/* gcc defines __powerpc__ on 64-bit PowerPC as well, so this has to exclude
+   __powerpc64__ explicitly; otherwise both blocks below fire and MACHINE_TYPE
+   and CURRENT_FASL_ARCH are each defined twice.  */
+#if defined(__powerpc__) && !defined(__powerpc64__)
 #  define __ppc__ 1
 #endif
 
@@ -586,6 +589,7 @@ extern void win32_stack_reset (void);
 #ifdef __ppc64__
 #  define MACHINE_TYPE		"PowerPC-64"
 #  define CURRENT_FASL_ARCH	FASL_PPC64
+#  define HEAP_IN_LOW_MEMORY	1
 #endif
 
 #ifdef __x86_64__
